WEBVTT

00:00:04.809 --> 00:00:09.710
<v Callum Reid>Morning, all. Can everyone hear me? Teams reckons half of you are still joining.</v>

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:14.730
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, we're here. It's just thinking about it.</v>

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:21.879
<v Sarah Okafor>Before we start, whose new car is that in the car park? Very shiny for this place.</v>

00:00:24.059 --> 00:00:29.660
<v Jamie Brennan>Someone's new car in the car park and you've already clocked it. Nothing gets past you.</v>

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.950
<v Sarah Okafor>It's taking up enough room to count as a small department.</v>

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.250
<v Marcus Hale>Not mine. Mine's the one held together by road dirt.</v>

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:45.729
<v Jamie Brennan>I parked beside it. Felt like I ought to apologise to it.</v>

00:00:46.509 --> 00:00:48.609
<v David Whitfield>For your parking or your car?</v>

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:51.920
<v Jamie Brennan>Both, probably.</v>

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.530
<v Callum Reid>Right, excellent. Vehicle assessment complete. Let's do the factory.</v>

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.399
<v Priya Raman>Yep. Morning.</v>

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:05.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Just a completed one from me: signed off the inspection on the GT1 Compressor Section on Tuesday. That's all sorted.</v>

00:01:07.079 --> 00:01:09.530
<v Callum Reid>Cheers. Nothing outstanding on that inspection, then.</v>

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.500
<v Sarah Okafor>No, signed off and finished.</v>

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:19.689
<v Callum Reid>Pricey, the near miss at the Line 2 Safety Guard Interlock needs writing up.</v>

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:27.750
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll write up the near miss at the Line 2 Safety Guard Interlock by Thursday.</v>

00:01:29.579 --> 00:01:32.030
<v Callum Reid>Thanks, Pricey. Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:36.510
<v Hannah Price>Understood. That takes priority; by Thursday for the write-up.</v>

00:01:37.569 --> 00:01:41.069
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, you clipped out just after 'near miss' for me.</v>

00:01:42.829 --> 00:01:45.629
<v Hannah Price>Line 2 Safety Guard Interlock. The near-miss write-up.</v>

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:47.459
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Got you. Audio's back.</v>

00:01:48.879 --> 00:01:50.980
<v Callum Reid>Lovely. Whitty, over to your side.</v>

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:58.530
<v Callum Reid>Can you investigate the pressure drop on the GT2 water valve? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:00.849 --> 00:02:05.400
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, I'll take that. Investigate the pressure drop on the GT2 water valve.</v>

00:02:05.739 --> 00:02:09.939
<v Marcus Hale>Pressure drop, yeah. Rather than assuming the valve itself is the culprit.</v>

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.419
<v David Whitfield>Exactly. Investigation first, not jumping straight to swapping bits.</v>

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.580
<v Callum Reid>That's it, Whitty. Worth understanding, but not an urgent call-out.</v>

00:02:20.389 --> 00:02:21.590
<v David Whitfield>Fine by me.</v>

00:02:22.659 --> 00:02:25.810
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, go on—you were about to say something else.</v>

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:34.419
<v David Whitfield>I was, yeah. I'll run a function test on the 11kV board as well. Low priority, that one.</v>

00:02:34.759 --> 00:02:38.259
<v Callum Reid>Okay, Whitty. Function test on the 11kV board, low priority.</v>

00:02:38.939 --> 00:02:40.689
<v Priya Raman>Function test, not changing anything?</v>

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:45.930
<v David Whitfield>Yep, just the function test. Nothing about altering settings.</v>

00:02:47.189 --> 00:02:48.389
<v Priya Raman>Right, understood.</v>

00:02:50.509 --> 00:02:52.960
<v Callum Reid>Okay. Stores Jamie, what have you got?</v>

00:02:55.379 --> 00:02:59.580
<v Jamie Brennan>I'll swap the filter on the line one HPU today at 2pm.</v>

00:03:00.659 --> 00:03:02.759
<v Sarah Okafor>Two o'clock today, did you say?</v>

00:03:05.099 --> 00:03:08.949
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, today at 2pm. The filter on the line one HPU.</v>

00:03:10.219 --> 00:03:11.969
<v Callum Reid>Thanks, stores Jamie. That's yours.</v>

00:03:12.409 --> 00:03:16.960
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep. Not just me talking about a filter, I'm actually doing that one.</v>

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:20.180
<v David Whitfield>We believed you. Mostly.</v>

00:03:20.819 --> 00:03:26.770
<v Callum Reid>And I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the gas valve on one on Friday.</v>

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Cal, that one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:03:33.439 --> 00:03:39.389
<v Callum Reid>Absolutely. Safety-critical priority straight away; on Friday is when the permit to work and isolation are required.</v>

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:44.810
<v Priya Raman>Right, Friday's the required date. I thought I'd missed a change there.</v>

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:52.710
<v Callum Reid>No change. I'll own the permit to work and isolation for the gas valve on one.</v>

00:03:53.219 --> 00:03:54.419
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, thanks, Cal.</v>

00:03:55.909 --> 00:03:58.710
<v Callum Reid>Marc? Think you were trying to come in.</v>

00:04:00.719 --> 00:04:06.319
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, so I'll do a site visit at the water works with the contractor after lunch.</v>

00:04:06.919 --> 00:04:11.819
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, Marc. That's an 'if you've got a spare minute' one, not a rush.</v>

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:17.970
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, understood. I'll take that after lunch, low-key rather than dropping everything.</v>

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:22.290
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I heard 'after lunch' about three times then. Someone's echoing.</v>

00:04:24.269 --> 00:04:28.470
<v Marcus Hale>Only said it once that time. I'm not that keen on lunch.</v>

00:04:29.889 --> 00:04:31.089
<v Jamie Brennan>You absolutely are.</v>

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:35.620
<v Callum Reid>Right. Anything unclear in what we've agreed?</v>

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.519
<v Hannah Price>No, all clear here.</v>

00:04:38.519 --> 00:04:39.720
<v David Whitfield>Same here.</v>

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:44.509
<v Callum Reid>Good stuff. Thanks, everyone. I'll let you get away.</v>
